  "definition": "Cold-gas propulsion produces thrust by opening a valve and expanding stored propellant through a nozzle. It uses no combustion or catalytic decomposition: the available pressure and enthalpy of the stored fluid provide the exhaust energy.[^1] Cold gas is therefore a non-reacting, pneumatic form of [[Spacecraft Propulsion]] in a mechanism-based ontology.",
